                  </coding>
               </code>
               <text>
                  <status value="generated"/>
                  <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the hospital course of your patient, a 40-year-old male, admitted on 16/12/2017 with acute right lower quadrant abdominal pain, nausea, and low-grade fever, clinically suspicious for appendicitis. On admission, physical examination confirmed peritoneal irritation at McBurney's point. Blood tests revealed leukocytosis consistent with acute inflammation. Abdominal ultrasound supported the diagnosis of acute appendicitis. The patient was promptly prepared for surgery, and a laparoscopic emergency appendectomy was performed on 16/12/2017 without intraoperative complications. Postoperatively, the patient received intravenous fluids, analgesics, and prophylactic antibiotics. Wound care was provided and recovery was uneventful. Vital signs remained stable throughout the stay. The patient was mobilized early and discharged home on 18/12/2017 in good general condition. Please follow up wound healing and histopathology results accordingly. Kind regards.</div>
               </text>
            </section>
